     "page": 1,
     "text": "CLINICAL SUMMARY - Valencia Butler and Gardner Medical Group\n\nPatient: Elizabeth Santiago DOB: 05/30/1958 Sex: F MRN: 200961\n\nEncounters:\n\n 2025-09-15 annual physical BP 149/82 Wt 223\n On September 15, 2025, Ms. Santiago visited for her annual physical examination. Her blood pressure was 149/82 mmHg, and she weighed 223 pounds at that time. The physical exam was otherwise unremarkable. She reported no new complaints and appeared in good overall health.\n\n 2025-04-23 ankle sprain BP 155/92 Wt 214\n On April 23, 2025, Ms. Santiago presented with an ankle sprain. blood pressure was recorded at 155/92 mmHg, and she weighed 214 pounds. The exam revealed an injured right ankle with swelling and tenderness. She was advised on rest, ice, compression, and elevation, and referred to physical therapy as needed. She also reported mild ankle on ambulation, which was otherwise normal.\n\n 2024-11-28 Benign tumor / polyps BP 157/88 Wt 222\n On November 28, 2024, Ms. Santiago visited for a follow-up regarding her benign tumors and polyps. Her blood pressure was 157/88 mmHg, and she weighed 222 pounds. During the exam, she had no new gastrointestinal symptoms or abdominal pain. The previous polyps were stable, and no new lesions were found. She continues to be monitored regularly.\n\n 2024-07-06 Cancer (see type table) BP 153/86 Wt 225\n On July 6, 2024, Ms. Santiago had a routine follow-up for her acute leukemia, which has been controlled for approximately 13.3 years following treatment. Her blood pressure was 153/86 mmHg, and she weighed 225 pounds at the time. A complete blood count, bone marrow biopsy, and imaging studies showed no signs of recurrence. She reported no new symptoms related to her cancer.\n\n 2024-02-11 Benign tumor / polyps BP 146/85 Wt 216\n On February 11, 2024, Ms. Santiago returned for monitoring of her benign tumors and polyps. Her blood pressure was 146/85 mmHg, and she weighed 216 pounds. Physical examination showed no abnormalities. Colonoscopy findings were stable, with no new polyps or concerning lesions detected. She continues to be followed periodically.\n\n 2023-09-18 Benign tumor / polyps BP 144/93 Wt 229\n On September 18, 2023, Ms. Santiago underwent a follow-up visit for her benign tumors and polyps. Her blood pressure was 144/93 mmHg, and she weighed 229 pounds at that time. The physical exam was otherwise unremarkable. Colonoscopy revealed stable polyps without dysplasia. She remains under regular surveillance.\n\nAssessment/Plan:\n\n• Acute leukemia, stage not stated (status post-treatment approximately 1"
    },
