     "page": 2,
     "text": "3.3 years ago) - controlled; meds: none\nMs. Santiago’s acute leukemia, diagnosed in 2011, has remained in remission for over 13 years following treatment. Currently, she is not on any medications for her cancer and shows no signs of recurrence.\n\n• Benign tumor / polyps - controlled; meds: none\nMs. Santiago has a history of benign tumors and polyps, which have been controlled. She has not required any medications for this condition, and her follow-up colonoscopies have shown no concerning findings.\n\nSocial: alcohol ~3 drinks/week\nMs. Santiago reports consuming approximately three alcoholic drinks per week. She has no history of smoking or other substance abuse. She is generally compliant with her medical follow-up and reports no significant lifestyle changes that could impact her health.\n"
